# Public functions whose own doc-comment states a sentinel contract,
# per module. The `Result` migration's size, and its DIRECTION.
#
# `docs/error-model.md` sizes this with a `grep` proxy over
# `errno|sentinel|(- 0 1)` and tells the reader to recompute rather
# than quote. Recomputed 2026-08-26 that proxy reads 89 over 15 files,
# not the 64 recorded - and around sixty of those are COMMENT lines.
# `stdlib/IO.ax` has eleven matches and zero in code. A per-file "no
# file may rise" rule over that metric would gate PROSE, and the
# migration's own explanatory comments would break it on the first
# commit.
#
# So the unit here is a public FUNCTION, which is what the migration
# ports and what a caller depends on. `scripts/check-compat.sh`
# recomputes these and refuses any file that RISES. A file may fall
# freely - that is the migration - and the number here is lowered in
# the same commit that lowers the count.
#
# R5: gate the direction before porting anything.
stdlib/Agent/Tags.ax 3
stdlib/IO.ax 8
stdlib/Intern.ax 1
stdlib/Path.ax 2
stdlib/Str.ax 2
stdlib/Sys.ax 13
stdlib/Sys/Platform.darwin.ax 1
